{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkdEb4RXFqqHrDxGNEyA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've decided not to put money in yet. I'll ask you first, or go to the bank. If I went with what the page says, it would be an account at **פסגות** (Psagot) and the fund **\"אי.בי.אי. מחקה ת\"א 125 (4A)\"**. After 10 years I'd have about **86,045 ₪**. I'm only fairly sure, because those figures aren't for my money. The page started with 10,000 ₪ now and 500 ₪ a month, and \"תשואה בשנה 7%\" (return per year) was already filled in. I didn't touch the sliders. On those numbers you put in 70,000 ₪ and are left with 86,045. That's not much more for ten years of shares. It also says \"בכסף של היום\" (in today's money), and I'm not sure what that does to the figure.\n\n**What I looked at, in order:**\n1. **The first screen.** The title is \"איפה ואיך הכי זול להשקיע במדד\" (where and how to invest in an index most cheaply). Under it there's a row of English buttons: MSCI, S&P, נאסד\"ק. Normally I'd have left there. Because of the task I stayed, and \"ת\"א-125\" was already selected. The line \"קרנות ישראליות שמחזיקות את המניות\" (Israeli funds that hold the shares) I understood.\n2. **The result box.** \"הפקדתם 70,000 ₪\" (you deposited). Next to it, \"הבחירה שלכם · הזול\" (your choice, the cheapest) with 86,045 ₪. There's also another box with \"‎−1,030 ₪\", and I backed away from it. Under that is a coloured bar and a list of fees with coloured dots I couldn't tell apart: \"דמי משמרת\" (I don't know that term), \"עמלת זו על זו\", account fees, fund fees and \"מס\" (tax).\n3. **The fund name.** Below that it says Psagot, and \"מה החשבון גובה ב־10 שנים: 1,049 ₪\" (what the account charges over 10 years). Under that was the fund name.\n4. **The list of banks.** Psagot is first. Leumi, Hapoalim, Discount and Mercantile come out around 79,000–83,000 ₪, and the bank fees are 4,500–8,300 ₪. So yes, the banks take more. Hapoalim has a different price for \"לנשים מגיל 60\" (women over 60), but it says \"סגור למצטרפים\" (closed to new customers) and \"לא בחישוב\" (not in the calculation). That one bothered me.\n5. **Further down.** Altshuler and Meitav show red bars and about 63,000–65,000 ₪, and some at the bottom say \"אין נתון\" (no data). That's where I stopped, after six screens. I didn't read the rest.\n\n**What I didn't understand:**\n- \"מחקה\" and \"(4A)\"\n- \"דמי משמרת\"\n- \"עמלת זו על זו\"\n- \"בכסף של היום\"\n- The purple dotted lines under every number\n- The red, orange and yellow bars, which I couldn't read\n- \"אי.בי.אי.\" is the fund's name, but in the account list it's 11th, at 78,204 ₪, with a big red stripe. It confused me that the cheapest account is Psagot but the fund is from אי.בי.אי.\n\n**What was hard to read:** The pale grey text on the dark background, like \"הבחירה שלכם; האתר לא ממליץ על מדד\" (your choice; the site doesn't recommend an index). The long lines in small print were hard too.\n\n**Where I got worried:**\n- Lots of numbers on one screen, the minus sign and the red.\n- No one says whether this is as safe as a deposit. It's shares.\n- I didn't find who stands behind the site, \"מקור\".\n\n**What I would change:**\n- Let me put in my own amount and say it in plain words before all the numbers.\n- Don't start with English letters.\n- Use bigger, brighter text.\n- Explain in one sentence why the fund is called אי.בי.אי. when the account is Psagot."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1876,"cache_read_input_tokens":13423,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1876},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1660406f-916c-4e4d-b8ea-90d7b0e32d7e","uuid":"190d